      "username": "lugaru",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lugaru/{size}/2767_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-06-08T18:26:51.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So I was playing a little Magic the gathering with a blue/white deck, this one to be specific.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://wiki.mtgsalvation.com/article/Spectral_Legions\" class=\"onebox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://wiki.mtgsalvation.com/article/Spectral_Legions</a></p>\n<p>So somehow I was able to lay down 9 Plains before I put down my frist Island. Just the odds of that blow my mind. With most other decks I would have lost but when you combine Pacify, Ghostly Possession and Spirit Mantle you have a very defensive, stalling deck.</p>\n<p>Do you guys have any weird luck stories?</p>\n<p>I have a hard time remembering all the bad rolls from before college when we used to play RPG’s (lots of critical failures ending up in lifelong injuries) but I do remember my ability to roll 111 again and again in risk.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
