      "created_at": "2012-06-12T18:13:19.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Game of Pandemic a few weeks ago. 4 players. First player’s turn pulled up an Epidemic, which, due to the initial setup (three neighboring cities started with lots of counters), resulted in us immediately being hit with more than 8 Outbreaks - game over. Second player never even had a chance to start her turn…  :o</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;TheJayMann&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"TheJayMann\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>1:79999</p>\n<p>There are many things more unlikely than that, I think.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah, it just <span class=\"bbcode-i\">seems</span> impossible. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>Rabit</p>",
